      "problem": "If $S=\\{5,10,11,23,34,38\\}$ and $T=\\{17,21,23,38,43\\},$ then $S\\cap T=$",
      "worked_solution": "The set $S\\cap T$ is the set of all elements belonging to both $S$ and $T.$ Since $S$ and $T$ have only the elements $23$ and $38$ in common, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S\\cap T & =\\{5,10,11,23,34,38\\}\\cap \\{17,21,23,38,43\\} \\\\  & =\\{23,38\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
